<title>CHINA: China Jan-March sugar output up 13.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>China Jan-March sugar output up 13.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>China produced 4.112 million tonnes of sugar in the first three months of this year, up 13.6 percent from the same period of 1996, said a report issued by the State Statistical Bureau on Monday.</p>
<p>China produced 1.024 million tonnes of sugar in March alone, the report said without giving year-ago figures.</p>
<p>China's sugar crushing season is from October to April.</p>
<p>--Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
